  "prefLabel": "Plc 1200 COURT REPORTERS",
  "recordType": "rule-chapter",
  "ruleText": "CHAPTER Plc 1200 COURT REPORTERS\n\nStatutory Authority: RSA 310-A:164; RSA 310:6, II\n\nREVISION NOTE:\n\nPursuant to 2022, 64:1 and 64:2, effective 7-19-22, the Board of Court Reporters was renamed and re-established as the Advisory Board of Court Reporters under RSA 310-A:162, I and RSA 310-A:163. The former rulemaking authority of the Board of Court Reporters was transferred to the Executive Director of the Office of Professional Licensure and Certification (OPLC) under RSA 310-A:164.\n\nThe Executive Director adopted Chapter Plc 1200 governing court reporters as an interim rule in Document #13547, effective 2-1-23. The Executive Director subsequently adopted and filed Document #13585, effective 3-23-33, repealing Chapter Rep 100 through Chapter Rep 500 of the former Board of Court Reporters. The repeal of Chapter Rep 100 through Chapter Rep 500 meant that Document #13547 containing Chapter Plc 1200 replaced all prior filings affecting rules of the former Board of Court Reporters.\n\nThe filings prior to Document #13585 which affected the former Chapter Rep 100 through Rep 500 included the following documents, where italics indicate the rules were subject to expiration only pursuant to RSA 541-A:17, II:",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1200.html"
}
